message.content:
This appears to come from a CBP ruling on a festive-articles costume. Costumes of textile materials are classified in 9505.90 (festive articles) when they are not well-made wearing apparel. A costume made up of a tunic, collar, cuffs, belt, headpiece and mask, put up as a set, would be classified as a festive article under heading 9505.

The subheading is 9505.90.6000 for "Other festive, carnival or other entertainment articles." Under the older HTSUS, 9505.90.60 covered "Other," and the costume sets were classified there. A mask would be 9505.90.4000, but in a set the whole is classified under the component giving the essential character, and here that is the costume as a whole under 9505.90.6000.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The multi-piece Anubis costume set (tunic, collar, cuffs, belt, headpiece, mask) is not well-made wearing apparel and is classified as a festive/carnival entertainment article in heading 9505, subheading 9505.90.60."}
